        "explanation": "<p>The inversion of a <b>perfect fifth</b> ($C$ to $G$) is a <b>perfect fourth</b> ($G$ to $C$). Inverting an interval involves flipping the order of the notes, and the sum of the original interval and its inversion is always $9$ (e.g., $5 + 4 = 9$).</p>",
